          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Nuclear Energy: Summary and Context"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This unit has explored the atomic nucleus—from its structure to the tremendous energy it can release. Nuclear physics underlies technologies from medical imaging to power generation, and understanding it helps us make informed decisions about energy, health, and the environment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Key Concept: ",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This summary lesson brings together all the key ideas from atomic physics: atomic structure, radioactivity, half-life, uses and hazards of radiation, fission, and fusion. Use it to consolidate your understanding and identify any areas that need revision."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Equations and Relationships"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Atomic Structure"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "text"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "| Quantity | Formula | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| Mass number | A = Z + N | Protons + Neutrons |\n| Atomic number | Z | Number of protons |\n| Neutrons | N = A − Z | Mass number minus protons |"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Radioactive Decay"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "text"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "| Equation | Meaning |\n|----------|--------|\n| $^A_Z X \\rightarrow ^{A-4}_{Z-2} Y + ^4_2 \\alpha$ | Alpha decay |\n| $^A_Z X \\rightarrow ^A_{Z+1} Y + ^0_{-1} \\beta$ | Beta decay |\n| $^A_Z X^* \\rightarrow ^A_Z X + \\gamma$ | Gamma emission |"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Half-Life"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "N = N_0 \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where n = number of half-lives = t/t₁/₂"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Nuclear Energy"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "E = mc^2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "E = \\Delta m \\times c^2"
          }
        ]
      },
